' PAL — State diagram for UC-07: Booking lifecycle (pickup + return handover)
@startuml PAL_State_UC07_Booking_Handover

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #444
skinparam StateBackgroundColor #FDF6E3
skinparam StateBorderColor #333
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #888
hide empty description

title UC-07 — Booking state machine (pickup and return handover)

' ====== Top-level Booking states (declared explicitly) ======
state PaidPickupPending
state Active
state Returned
state Settled
state Cancelled

[*] --> PaidPickupPending : Booking created by UC-06

' ====== PICKUP VARIANT (composite) ======
state HandoverInProgress {
  [*] --> PhotosUploading
  PhotosUploading --> AwaitingBorrowerConfirm : photos >= 3 uploaded\n/ notify borrower via code/NFC
  PhotosUploading --> PhotosUploading : fewer than 3 photos\n/ block and ask for more (alt 3a)
  AwaitingBorrowerConfirm --> [*] : borrower agrees\n/ attach PhotoSet(variant=Pickup)
  AwaitingBorrowerConfirm --> Disputed : borrower disagrees\n/ open dispute case (alt 5a)
  Disputed : Booking state unchanged\nuntil dispute resolution
}

PaidPickupPending --> HandoverInProgress : lender starts handover\n/ prompt for 3 or more photos
HandoverInProgress --> Active : composite exits via final\n(happy path)

' ====== RETURN VARIANT (composite) ======
state ReturnInProgress {
  [*] --> PhotosUploadingR
  PhotosUploadingR : (return photos)
  PhotosUploadingR --> AwaitingBorrowerConfirmR : photos >= 3 uploaded\n/ notify borrower via code/NFC
  PhotosUploadingR --> PhotosUploadingR : fewer than 3 photos\n/ block and ask for more (alt 3a)
  AwaitingBorrowerConfirmR --> [*] : borrower agrees\n/ attach PhotoSet(variant=Return),\nstart deposit settlement (UC-07a)
  AwaitingBorrowerConfirmR --> DisputedR : borrower disagrees\n/ open dispute case (alt 5a)
  DisputedR : Booking state unchanged\nuntil dispute resolution
}

Active --> ReturnInProgress : lender starts return handover\n/ prompt for 3 or more photos
ReturnInProgress --> Returned : composite exits via final\n(happy path)

Returned --> Settled : deposit settlement completed (UC-07a)\n/ release held funds
Settled  --> [*]

' ====== Cross-UC edges to UC-09 ======
PaidPickupPending --> Cancelled : (cross-UC, UC-09) user cancels\nor borrower no-show window elapsed (alt 6a)
Active            --> Cancelled : (cross-UC, UC-09) dispute resolution\ncancels an active booking (rare)
Cancelled --> [*]

note right of HandoverInProgress
  Pickup variant (UC-07 Basic Flow 1-7).
  Exit via final pseudo-state moves the
  Booking to Active. The Disputed substate
  keeps the outer Booking state at
  PaidPickupPending until resolution.
end note

note left of ReturnInProgress
  Return variant (UC-07 Basic Flow 1-7,
  variant = Return). Successful exit
  triggers UC-07a (deposit settlement)
  and moves the Booking to Returned.
end note

note bottom
  Source: UC-07.
  The borrower-no-show branch (UC-07 alt 6a)
  routes PaidPickupPending to Cancelled after
  the no-show window; represented here as a
  second condition on the UC-09 cross-edge.
  Cross-UC edges to Cancelled are annotated in
  their labels (UC-09 owns the actual lifecycle).

  Operational (non-enum) states introduced per
  state_plan.md:
   * HandoverInProgress, ReturnInProgress (composite)
   * PhotosUploading / AwaitingBorrowerConfirm / Disputed
  The return-variant substates are suffixed with "R"
  only because PlantUML requires globally unique
  identifiers; semantically they mirror the pickup
  substates.
end note

@enduml
